# What this repository publishes is code. Everything below is excluded on
# purpose, and each block says why -- an exclusion nobody can explain is one
# somebody eventually deletes.
#
# NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS FILE: .gitignore has NO trailing comments.
# A '#' only starts a comment at the START of a line. Writing
#     uploads/    # screenshots
# makes the pattern the whole literal string, which matches nothing -- and it
# looks completely correct while doing it. That bug was in this file's first
# draft and it silently published 55 MB of screenshots. Keep comments on their
# own lines.

# ---- The memory. Personal, and the reason this list exists. ----------------
# The Obsidian vault: profile, dated session logs, email briefs, task queue.
# README step 6 tells a reader how to build their own. GitHub retains history
# even after a delete, so this line has to be right the FIRST time.
Jarvis-brain/

# ---- Anything else that is a record of a person rather than a program ------
# uploads/ is screenshots of my own screen (~55 MB).
# visual-server.log carries usage percentages and fragments of conversation.
#
# transcripts/ is 320 KB of VERBATIM, timestamped voice conversations. It is
# not code, and it was very nearly published: it survived the first exclusion
# list because that list was built from an inventory that never mentioned it.
#
# references/ holds design references, and one of them is a screenshot of my
# own Claude account showing plan tier and live usage percentages. Excluded
# whole rather than file by file -- an allow-list of images is a rule somebody
# has to re-apply every time a new one lands, and that is how this got missed.
uploads/
archive/
.scratch/
*.log

# Live state the running stack writes INTO the tree. Found 2026-08-06 by a
# see-page test that scans the repo for stray files: `.voice_question` was
# untracked and committable, and this repo is public. Everything here is
# runtime state, never source.
voice-line/.voice_question
voice-line/.stack-events.jsonl
voice-line/.sessions.jsonl
voice-line/.session-mail.jsonl
voice-line/.usage.json
transcripts/
references/

# ---- Live state. Written by the running stack, meaningless to a clone. -----
# Session registry, session bus, stack event log, usage readings.
voice-line/.sessions.jsonl
voice-line/.session-mail.jsonl
voice-line/.stack-events.jsonl
voice-line/.board-guard.json
voice-line/.usage.json
voice-line/.voice_transcript
# What each session is doing right now. Live state AND it carries session
# ids and pids -- this repo is public, so it is excluded for both reasons.
voice-line/.activity.json

# ---- Large, and reproducible from the README rather than from git ---------
# whisper GGML weights ~465 MB (install step 3); kokoro-fastapi ~1.5 GB
# (step 4); the uv venv (step 2); public-domain ambient tracks ~41 MB (step 5).
voice-line/models/
voice-line/services/
voice-line/.venv/
Jarvis Visual/audio/

# ---- The Discord line's credentials and local state ------------------------
# .token is the bot token -- a credential, never published. config.json holds
# the channel id and the family's Discord user ids -- personal, and this repo
# is public. config.example.json IS committed and is the template both are
# filled from by hand, on this machine only. bot.log is caught by *.log above;
# .bot.pid is runtime state.
discord-line/.token
discord-line/config.json
discord-line/.bot.pid

# ---- Build and OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# ---- Deliberately NOT ignored, so nobody adds them later by reflex --------
# uv.lock                 the pinned dependency set -- the point of a lock file
# CLAUDE.md               the boot file, shipped as a worked example
# templates/              the source the rendered files below are made from

# ---- Rendered from templates/ by install.sh, never committed --------------
# These carry an absolute path that is correct only on the machine that made
# them. templates/claude-settings.json.template is the single source for BOTH,
# so the two files cannot drift apart -- the property a test used to have to
# prove is now structural.
.claude/settings.json
Jarvis Visual/.claude/settings.json

# Serge's own brain-deck example, handed over 2026-08-12. A byte-identical
# copy is kept in Jarvis Visual/references/ (itself ignored). His file, and
# this repo is public -- it must never be published by a stray `git add .`.
jarvis-os/test.html
